1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
In this walkthrough we build a cohort in PIC-SURE from start to finish.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,500
First we search for a concept, blood pressure, and look at the variables each study offers for it.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:18,000
Each result shows the study, the variable name and how many participants have a value for it.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,500
We add systolic blood pressure as a filter and drag the range slider to keep values above one forty.

5
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:31,000
The participant count at the top updates straight away, so we can see the effect of every filter.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,500
Next we add a categorical filter for smoking status and tick the current and former smoker values.

7
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:44,000
Filters combine with AND by default, so the cohort shrinks with each filter we add to it.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,500
To combine filters with OR instead, we drag one filter onto another and they become a group.

9
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:57,000
Groups can be nested two levels deep, which covers most of the cohort definitions we see in practice.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,500
Now the cohort looks right, so we save it before doing anything else with it.

11
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:08,000
Unsaved filters are cleared when you sign out, which is the most common way people lose a cohort.

12
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,500
With the cohort saved, we open the export tab and pick the variables to include in the dataset.

13
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:21,000
We choose the workspace to export into; it needs a billing project, or the export will fail.

14
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:27,500
Large exports run in the background, and an email arrives when the dataset is ready, usually within ten minutes.

15
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:34,000
The exported dataset is named after the date and the cohort, so it is easy to find in the workspace.

16
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:40,500
Remember that authorized access exports only include the studies you are approved for.

17
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:47,000
That is why the participant count can drop between the open access view and the exported dataset.

18
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,500
To change the cohort later, reopen it from the saved cohorts list, edit the filters and export again.

19
00:01:53,500 --> 00:02:00,000
That is the whole cycle: search, filter, save, export, and analyze the dataset in your workspace.
